<div class = "container">
    <h1> Welcome! We're Glad You're Here</h1>
    <div class = "content-box">
        <p>
            Welcome to Momentum, a clean and intentional space designed to help you take control of your daily routines and building lasting, healthy habits. Whether you're trying to stay on top of your fitness, focus on personal wellness goals, or manage a busy acadmic schedule, tracking your consistency to build discipline is the first step toward real change and reaching your goal.</p>

        <p>
            Navigating the site is simple. You can use the navigation bar at the top of the page to move between pages. The dashboard is your main command center where all of your active habits are displayed in clean cards layout. If you want to get some motivation or read about some tips for building good habits, you can head over to the Motivation Blog page. If you want to learn about my inspiration for this project, head over to the About page. During the process if you need to drop a question or provide feeback, the Contact page is just a click away. </p>

        <p>
            To start building your momentum, navigate to the Dashboard page and click the "Create a New Habit" button. This will open up a form where you can name your habit, assign it a custom category like Fitness or Nutrition and set how often you would like to complete it. Once you fill out all the fields and click submit, a new card will pop up on your dashboard with that information. For each habit, you can easily check it off your list by clicking "Mark As Complete" when you finish it, or use "Edit" or "Delete" buttons to update your goals as your routine changes.</p>

        <p>
            Ultimately, I designed Momentum to take the guesswork out of your daily routine so you can focus entirely on your personal growth. By keeping tracking clean and simple, you can easily monitor your consistency without feeling overwhelmed. Whether you are using this to manage your health, stay on top of your studies, or create better daily disciplines, every habit you log brings you closer to your goals. I hope Momentum becomes a useful tool in your daily life as you work toward building better and healthier routines, one log at a time.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>